// The engine↔game contract (L1). The engine DECLARES the seam as a typed
// interface; a game provides the one `implement` block (its manifest,
// games/<game>/config/game.emp) binding each member to a symbol or value. This
// module emits nothing — it is pure declaration. The engine names members
// qualified (`Game.MEMBER`, `#Game.entry`) and calls hooks with
// `invoke Game.hook`, which lowers to an absolute `jsr` when a game binds the
// hook and to ZERO bytes when the hook stays `= empty`.
//
// GameState (the state-dispatch proc type the `entry` member is typed by) is
// `pub type`-declared in engine.game_loop, its dispatch-use home; the bind pass
// resolves member types across the whole reachable module set, so the interface
// consumes it without a cross-module type import (contract types are module-local
// by the import model).
module engine.game_contract

pub interface Game {
    // Comptime feature gate the engine's lowering consumes: the camera's
    // landing-lock arms comptime-select on it (a `CAMERA_JUMP_LOCK = false` game
    // gets the plain deadzone follow).
    const CAMERA_JUMP_LOCK: bool

    // The parallax capability mask (Scanline Services §3): which scanline services
    // ANY scene in this game demands, ORed across the game's whole scene registry.
    // A GAME-level fact by construction — one tier above acts, two above sections —
    // because the P2 lowering has to decide what machinery to OMIT before any section
    // is known, and a per-section value cannot answer that question.
    //
    // Derived-and-verified, never hand-maintained-unchecked: a game's scene registry
    // folds its scenes through fold_caps() (engine/level/scene_dsl.emp) and an ensure
    // there proves the fold is a SUBSET of this declaration. The direction is the
    // safety property — a declared SUPERSET only forgoes a specialisation, while a
    // declared subset would drop machinery a scene still demands.
    //
    // Typed u16 for the end state, not for today's reach: P1 defines five bits up to
    // $0010, and the P3+ bits reserved in scene_dsl.emp reach $0800. Note the width is
    // documentary — sigil's contract checker range-checks no const member, only that
    // the bound value is int-ish — so the registry's ensure is the whole guard.
    //
    // NO ENGINE CONSUMER EXISTS YET. Unlike every other member here, nothing reads
    // `Game.SCANLINE_CAPS`, so it lowers to nothing and moves no ROM byte; it is
    // contract surface that the scene registry can be checked against. The comptime
    // arms that make these bits load-bearing arrive in P2.
    const SCANLINE_CAPS: u16

    // The boot handoff: the first game-state routine and its state id. Boot ends
    // with `move.l #Game.entry, (Game_State).w` + `move.b #Game.ENTRY_ID, ...`.
    const ENTRY_ID: u8
    proc entry: GameState

    // Engine-invoked, game-implemented hooks. `= empty` declares the default —
    // an unbound hook's call site emits NOTHING (empty costs zero bytes, the
    // canonical-shape invariant).
    //
    // boot_hook: engine boot invokes this after Sound_Init, before the game-state
    // handoff. clobbers(d0-d4/a0-a1) is the honest bound: sonic4's
    // SoundTest_BootPing calls Sound_PlayMusic (clobbers d0-d4/a0-a1), whose
    // d2-d4 leak past the ping's own d0/a0 — a generous boot-time bound (every
    // register is free post-boot) that the real impl satisfies exactly.
    hook boot_hook () clobbers(d0-d4/a0-a1) = empty

    // debug_tick: engine GameLoop invokes this once per frame after VSync/SFX
    // drain. ⊤ (d0-d7/a0-a6) — it runs beside the GameState dispatch's own ⊤
    // bound; sonic4's Debug_MusicToggle (clobbers d0-d4/a0-a1) sits inside it.
    hook debug_tick () clobbers(d0-d7/a0-a6) = empty

    // ring_collected: RingCollision (engine/objects/rings.emp) invokes this once per
    // collected ring, AFTER the collect bookkeeping (collected bit, loaded bit,
    // Ring_Counter, SFX) and BEFORE RingBuffer_Remove, with a3 = the ring's buffer
    // entry (X.w at +0, Y.w at +2 — the engine-space centre — then section_id.b,
    // list_index.b; RING_BUFFER_ENTRY_SIZE bytes). The entry is still valid at the
    // call. A game binds its collect visual here (sonic4: RingSparkle_Spawn); the demo
    // leaves it `= empty`. Handing the POINTER rather than loading X/Y into d0/d1 on
    // the engine side keeps the unbound case at exactly zero bytes (the demo ROM is
    // byte-identical with or without the hook). The bound is the spawner's exact need
    // (AllocEffect's d0/a1 + two coords) and deliberately excludes every register
    // RingCollision holds live across the collect path (a2/a3 cursors, d4-d7 player
    // coords and loop counters) — a3 in particular is an INPUT the hook must preserve.
    hook ring_collected (a3: *u8) clobbers(d0-d2/a1) = empty
}
